      "answer": "According to Cargo's official documentation, Cargo.lock is used to record the exact versions of dependencies used in a build — \"Cargo.lock contains exact information about your dependencies.\" It is maintained by Cargo (not manually edited) and ensures reproducible builds by pinning the precise dependency versions.\n\nSources:\n- \n- \n\nFINAL LABEL: supported\n\nSources:\n- https://dev-doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/guide/cargo-toml-vs-cargo-lock.html\n- https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-generate-lockfile.html\n- https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/guide/cargo-toml-vs-cargo-lock.html\n- https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/cargo/guide/cargo-toml-vs-cargo-lock.html",
