      "completed": true,
      "answer": "**Report preserved:** `.smara/sessions/session/artifacts/d843e48364cd871edafbf727d2d6f088846ab5a9e3a4008bdac4b2aa5f220df3.md` (10,287 chars, 24 fetched sources, 6/6 claims validated).\n\n## Summary\n\n**Exact PEP title:** PEP 621 — **\"Storing project metadata in pyproject.toml\"** (Status: Final, Standards Track, Packaging; created 22-Jun-2020).\n\n**Purpose:** Its abstract states verbatim: *\"This PEP specifies how to write a project's core metadata in a pyproject.toml file for packaging-related tools to consume.\"* It standardizes a static, tool-agnostic `[project]` table so all build back-ends read the same metadata deterministically without executing Python code.\n\n**How packaging tools consume it:** PEP 518 front-ends (pip, build) read the `[build-system]` table, install the declared back-end into an isolated environment, and invoke PEP 517 hooks; the back-end (setuptools, Hatchling, Flit-core, PDM-backend) then reads the `[project]` table — *\"The keys defined in this specification MUST be in a table named [project] in pyproject.toml\"* — validates it, and converts it into RFC 822-style wheel/sdist METADATA. Poetry-core historically used `[tool.poetry]` instead of the standard table.\n\n**Key sources:**\n- https://peps.python.org/pep-0621\n- https://github.com/python/peps/blob/main/peps/pep-0621.rst\n- https://packaging.python.org/en/latest/specifications/pyproject-toml\n- https://setuptools.pypa.io/en/stable/userguide/pyproject%5Fconfig.html\n- https://pdm-project.org/en/latest/reference/pep621\n- https://hatch.pypa.io/1.5/config/metadata\n\nFINAL LABEL: supported",
